            <ArticleTitle>Unexpected outcome after partial epididymectomy for chronic testicular pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>216-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Cancer of the testis is uncommon in young males. It can present in unusual ways. We are presenting a case of testicular cancer presenting as an epididymal lesion that was diagnosed after epididymectomy.</AbstractText>
